        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nCould you please more closely follow the 6a6a37ec54f833e2a733f5f04959f506520701ba? I.e. almost the same set of changes and the almost the same commit message.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> Shall I add the new mapping to MiniMax as `<leader>lx`?\r\n\r\nThis is a bit early for MiniMax. Let's wait until the Neovim 0.12 release.\r\n\r\nBesides, I am not sure that `<Leader>lx` is a good LHS. I would expect something like `<Leader>lc` (*C*odelens) or `<Leader>ll` (*L*ens; similar to how `<Leader>la` is \"*A*ctions\").",
