        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> > Shall I add the new mapping to MiniMax as `<leader>lx`?\r\n> \r\n> This is a bit early for MiniMax. Let's wait until the Neovim 0.12 release.\r\n> \r\n> Besides, I am not sure that `<Leader>lx` is a good LHS. I would expect something like `<Leader>lc` (_C_odelens) or `<Leader>ll` (_L_ens; similar to how `<Leader>la` is \"_A_ctions\").\r\n\r\nI've only now realized that `vim.lsp.codelens.run()` is not new and is present at least since Neovim>=0.10. So adding it to MiniMax can be done now. And I think the `<Leader>ll` fits more into the current language mapping convention.\r\n\r\nBut at the same time, I've never really used codelens, so there is no mapping for it already. Do you know any particularly good use for it? Enough to warrant the extra `<Leader>ll` mapping?",
